y of those routes i feel  like i'm the best  how much press coverage did you face in  college  uh  i faced a pretty good amount  um probably from almost every team  and and uh  have you gotten an idea of  you know what it's going to be like to  face press coverage when you're dealing  with an nfl caliber defensive back have  you gotten any work in that regard have  you gotten any specific advice on how  different it's going to be getting off  the line of scrimmage at that level  oh yes sir i've gotten some advice of  how they're going to play me  and then uh just playing in the sec  um i feel like that that's gotten me  more ready  for the next level than anything but i  know at the next level you know they're  just going to be a step better a step  quicker uh that much smarter  um than  the dbs in the sec so i'm just ready to  take on that challenge  well and one thing that helps you you've  got the size you've got the strength  you've got the physique to pull it off  to do battle hand to hand with those  defensive backs and you've created a lot  of buzz for the shape that you're in and  there was a suggestion that your body  fat is only one point six percent  somebody said it's impossible that  anyone's body fat percentage could be  that low do you know the actual number  of your body fat percentage  yes it was 1.9  oh it's 1.9 okay well okay  so one point  one point six a little bit off 1.9 is  the magic number for dk metcalf's body  fat percentage what do you what do you  give me your because i could use a  little lab work give me your best three  ab exercises to get as ripped as you are  um  they call rebel abs um like six inches  crunches and then uh you hold both of  them uh for a minute so  um in track my track coach had me do abs  almost every day so  i just used that ab workout  and as your abs got stronger as your  core got stronger how did you feel that  translated into your football game  um i could run forever  and then my my balance was pretty good  uh just coming from my core work so i  just kept doing abs  what's your favorite pass route to run  i go out  why  four three three  yes yes sir if i can  beat the defender off the line i don't  have to worry about him anymore  when you ran that four three three at  the con by me what were you expecting to  generate that day  um i thought i was gonna run a 438-435  um i did not expect to get uh below that  um but after i did you know i just thank  god for the opportunity thank god  because you know without him  um i wouldn't be able to do that so um i  was just after that enjoying the moment  with my family just ready to get back on  and let's go back to the go route when  you run 40 yards in a straight line you  don't have to worry about anybody  knocking you off the ball you don't have  to worry about looking for a ball are  there some nuances to because people  just think you just go right go route  nine routes straight down the field give  me an idea of what some of those details  are that people may not realize  you know watching a game on tv as to how  what it takes to get open  when you're when your assignment is  simply go straight down the field  um people don't realize that there's a  defender in front of you that you have  to manipulate or  try to get low and  uh try to trick them with your footwork  so um you know people don't see that  my feet are quick and i can get off  press coverage uh whenever i want to  so you know i just let the people talk  how much does the quarterback factor in  whether and to what extent it's going to  take you time to get off of press  coverage because if they jam you up for  a little bit it throws off the timing of  the whole play  right um so the quarterback has to see  where i'm at and throw a perfect ball  you know over the outside shoulder to  where only i can catch it or nobody  catches it so the quarterback plays a  big role in uh in that too  the uh you know the question always  comes up for the prospects in the draft  are you the best at your position the  answer is always yes so i'll assume your  answer is yes but i want you to tell me  what makes you the best receiving  prospect in the 2019 draft class  um  because of what i did at the combine and  then you know i feel like i can run  routes i can block and i can catch the  ball  um  so  there's no other complete receiver than  me in my mind  what's the question you got most often  from the teams that that spoke to you in  the weeks leading up to the draft  um probably about my injuries in uh  college  they asked what did you say  what what would be your explanation or  or what the information they wanted from  you as to the injuries that you suffered  um they're just freak injuries and could  happen to anybody  playing this sport but um you know i'm  i'm not injury prone or  any of that  and i'm just going to take care of my  body at the next level  is there a criticism of your game at the  college level that bugs you that you  think is unfair  um people saying that i had a limited  router  what what how how far does your route  tree go beyond the go route  uh a goal post  a curl  that's pretty much all we ran  is there one specific route that you  know you're going to need to work on to  to run it the way they're going to  expect you to run at the nfl level  probably the outro because  i just stick and i don't explode out i  just kind of like coached out so  probably the hour out  what receivers currently playing in the  nfl or that ever have played in the nfl  do you try to pattern yourself after  um the big receivers who can run as well  like julio calvin johnson and uh randy  moss  have you gotten advice from any of these  guys who have really done it at a high  level in the nfl as to what you need to  do to be like them  no sir i really haven't uh talked to  anybody  guys who have played at mississippi that  are at the next level any guys that  you've been working with  who may be back in school you have a  relationship with them like a la crosse  quan treadwell guys who can help you  understand what you're going to be  getting yourself into when you head to  the nfl  uh derek jones he was a cornerback at  the jets  gave me a lot of tips  um dante moncrief who's now the receiver  for the steelers  um he told me about uh press coverage  and you know the process  of leading up to the draft and you know  after the draft and then um evan ingram  uh has gave give me a lot of tips on you  know what to do when i get there  you're going to the draft on thursday  night in nashville what what are you  expecting that evening to be like for  you  um i'm really not expecting anything i'm  just gonna go in and whatever happens  happens uh just gonna let god take care  of it i'm just gonna gonna enjoy uh the  time of my family  do you have a range high and a low where  you you think maybe that's where you may  end up going  uh no sir no expectations at all  when that phone rings what do you think  your reaction is gonna be  i'm probably gonna bless out to cry  just knowing all of my hard work is just  it's going to pay off  and um  i i know that you've said before and and  and you have no choice but to say you're  going to go wherever you get drafted but  would you kind of prefer that maybe to  stay a little closer to home not go  quite so far away to start off your nfl  career it doesn't matter to you  no sir it really doesn't matter to me  because i know my family's going to be  there regardless  well uh dk we appreciate some of your  time as you get ready to embark on what  should be a very exciting journey we're  rooting for you and we can't wait to see  you run the go route and every other  route at the nfl level and uh we thank  old spice for giving us some of your  time today all the best on thursday  night we look forward to talking to you  down the road yes sir thank you  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc 